<h2 style=3D"color:#000;font:700 24px/31px nyt-cheltenham,georgia,serif;mar=
gin:0 0 10px"><span>The mysterious story of what didn=E2=80=99t happen at a=
 British air base</span></h2><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,seri=
f;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>At first, it seemed like a terrorist at=
tack on a British air base had been thwarted. Then the story turned strange=
r.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;mar=
gin:0 0 15px"><span>The five men arrested last week had been traveling in w=
hite vans in the middle of the night near a base in southern England that t=
he U.S. has used in its war against Iran. The Islamic Revolutionary Guards =
Corps had warned over the summer that =E2=80=9Cany base used to launch atta=
cks on Iranian territory=E2=80=9D would be =E2=80=9Ca legitimate target.=E2=
=80=9D The arrests suggested that threat had materialized.</span></p><p sty=
le=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span=
>But the details we=E2=80=99ve learned since then have been confusing. The =
men in the white vans=3F Not radicalized ideologues or hardened operators, =
but =E2=80=9C</span><a href=3D"https://nl.nytimes.com/f/newsletter/eld7GdLq=
UsrXEMx4eAh2tA~~/AAAAARA~/AYpJEHgK6Pger8LD3IVhaI4qiqM6nlxbeAgcroY__7_stuZiJ=
