dwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decoration:underline;text-decora=
tion:underline">unwitting chumps</a><span>,=E2=80=9D one official said. One=
 of them called emergency services himself; we still don=E2=80=99t know why=
=2E</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;ma=
rgin:0 0 15px"><span>Perhaps most mysterious of all is what the suspected p=
lot was meant to achieve. When the police searched the vans, they found som=
e gasoline but no explosives. The British prime minister, Andy Burnham, sai=
d there were =E2=80=9Cstrong indications that Iran played a part.=E2=80=9D =
But as my colleagues recently put it =E2=80=94 =E2=80=9Ca part in what, exa=
ctly=3F=E2=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;=
color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The men were soon released on bail =E2=80=
=94 not something that tends to happen with suspected terrorists. The whole=
 thing seemed odd, but mostly over, until this weekend, when the U.S. rushe=
d to remove its bombers based on what two U.S. officials called =E2=80=9Cne=
w threats.=E2=80=9D It has since emerged that the withdrawal was because of=
 the </span><a href=3D"https://nl.nytimes.com/f/newsletter/fjeZQujoV3fuScDl=
nfjWmg~~/AAAAARA~/eFdoMBXiXfH3gSeO1YolSvxWXML2n1peJ4sJeRIZtSbnC_ZoYLuAh_OrS=
